  "articleBody": "Choosing a general contractor for your home project doesn't have to be daunting if you know the right steps. It’s all about clear communication and thorough vetting. First off, you need to define your project's scope – what exactly do you want done? This clarity helps contractors provide accurate bids. Next, it’s crucial to ask for itemized pricing or, ideally, a fixed-price contract so you know exactly what you’re paying for. Don't settle for vague estimates! When you're talking to potential contractors, confirm who will be staffing the project and how supervision will be handled. A hands-on owner like Abraham Becerra of HH Remodeling LLC, based in Aurora, can be a real asset here, providing direct oversight. Establish a clear communication plan from the get-go; you want to know how you'll receive updates and who your primary contact will be. Finally, ensure all the details are documented: warranties, who handles permits and inspections, and a clear closeout process including punch-list completion and lien waivers. This structured approach helps ensure a smooth project, minimizes surprises, and leads to a successful renovation outcome with a trusted professional.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}